' Sharing a resource collection across threads is out of scope (spec §15.6), so a
' `RES`-marked collection on a thread's DATA plane is rejected with
' TYPE_THREAD_NOT_SENDABLE. The plane it sits on must not change that answer.
'
' bug-463: it did. The output plane is never measured — the thread grammar takes
' "everything after the last ` TO `" — but the MESSAGE plane has to be measured to
' find where it ends, and that measurement had no `RES ` arm. It stopped inside the
' element (after `List OF RES`), the ` TO ` split failed, and the entire spelling
' survived as one opaque nominal. The sendability rule never ran; the resolver
' rejected the junk name instead, reporting a package `Thread OF List OF RES fs`
' that never existed. The program was refused by an accident of spelling rather
' than by the rule that governs it.

IMPORT fs
IMPORT io

FUNC viaList(t AS Thread OF List OF RES fs::File TO Integer) AS Integer
  RETURN 0
END FUNC

FUNC viaMap(t AS Thread OF Map OF String TO RES fs::File TO Integer) AS Integer
  RETURN 0
END FUNC

FUNC viaWorker(t AS ThreadWorker OF List OF RES fs::File TO Integer) AS Integer
  RETURN 0
END FUNC

FUNC main AS Integer
  io::print("unreachable")
  RETURN 0
END FUNC
